      "body": "# What does this PR do?\n\nWith `packing: true` and `neat_packing: false`, `supervised.py` restarts each packed example's `position_ids` at `0` (since `c3c0efba`), while the attention mask still covers the whole pack. On SDPA/eager, and on FA2 with more than one pack per batch, later examples attend to earlier ones while their positions reset to `0`. This causes the high SFT packing loss in #8277.\n\n`Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct` (`flash_attn: auto`, 120 GSM8K examples in 13 packs of 2,048 tokens, 12,877 label tokens after the first example per pack):\n\n| setting | position restarts | later examples' mean NLL |\n|---|---|---|\n| alone / `neat_packing: true` | 0 | 0.694 |\n| unpatched `main` (`packing: true`) | 107 | 3.480 |\n| this PR (`packing: true`) | 0 | 0.430 |\n\nWith consistent positions, earlier GSM8K examples in the pack act as in-context examples.\n\nThis PR emits `0..L-1` over the pack when `neat_packing` is false (`neat_packing: true` is unchanged) and adds `test_supervised_packing_position_ids`.\n\nNotes:\n- On FA2 with `per_device_train_batch_size: 1`, `transformers` inferred varlen boundaries from the reset positions; plain packing now attends across the pack on all backends as documented (use `neat_packing: true` for isolated packing).\n- Existing `datasets` caches are not invalidated automatically; re-run with `overwrite_cache: true`.\n\nFixes #8277\n\n## Before submitting\n\n- [x] Did you read the [contributor guideline](https://github.com/hiyouga/LLaMA-Factory/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md)?\n- [x] Did you write any new necessary tests?\n",
